WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.140 --> 00:00:05.310
Hey youtubers it’s Charlie and they just
revealed that Arrow episode 4 is titled the

00:00:05.310 --> 00:00:08.769
Magician. They tweeted a copy of the title
page at the start of filming this morning.

00:00:08.769 --> 00:00:12.890
Marc Guggenheim included John Barrowman’s
name in the tweet so the title “The Magician”

00:00:12.890 --> 00:00:16.990
probably refers to Merlyn the Magician. But
it could also be an easter egg for Zatanna.

00:00:16.990 --> 00:00:23.109
Plus Guillermo Del Toro said he wanted to
include Constantine from the tv show in his

00:00:23.109 --> 00:00:25.689
Justice League Dark movie. So there’s a
lot of new talk of integration.

00:00:25.689 --> 00:00:29.960
This video is going to be an explanation of
Merlyn the Magician as in Malcolm Merlyn.

00:00:29.960 --> 00:00:33.670
Just because that’s what episode 4 is going
to be about. Magician is one of his nicknames

00:00:33.670 --> 00:00:39.840
and I’ll also do backstory for Zatanna,
Constantine and Doctor Fate and how the show

00:00:39.840 --> 00:00:42.059
might treat them if they ever ended up doing
a crossover.

00:00:42.059 --> 00:00:44.300
If this is the first time you’re finding
me I do Arrow and DC videos every week. Be

00:00:44.300 --> 00:00:46.059
sure to subscribe to get everything.

00:00:46.059 --> 00:00:50.129
So Magic on Arrow isn’t going to happen
just yet. I think it took Smallville 8 seasons

00:00:50.129 --> 00:00:53.690
to get to it. The Magician title of Episode
4 refers to Merlyn Malcolm.

00:00:53.690 --> 00:00:57.789
Malcolm Merlyn’s original name in the comics
before he joined the League of Assassins was

00:00:57.789 --> 00:01:02.940
Arthur King. Eventually he took the stage
name Merlyn the Magician. In Oliver Queen’s

00:01:02.940 --> 00:01:07.100
first few years as Green Arrow in Star City,
Arthur challenged him to a public archery

00:01:07.100 --> 00:01:10.810
contest. Arthur or Merlyn the Magician as
he called himself lost and in a rage, disappeared

00:01:10.810 --> 00:01:11.030
from public life.

00:01:11.030 --> 00:01:11.799
Eventually he became an assassin and trained
himself to perfection in case he ever crossed

00:01:11.799 --> 00:01:12.450
path with Green Arrow again. He took on his
Merlyn the Magician alias full time and left

00:01:12.450 --> 00:01:13.850
his old name Arthur King behind.

00:01:13.850 --> 00:01:17.490
Eventually he was recruited into the league
of assassins and during his time there he

00:01:17.490 --> 00:01:20.520
went on to tutor the Cassandra Cain batgirl.

00:01:20.520 --> 00:01:25.350
This was before the new 52 reboot. After the
reboot his real name was retconned to be Tommy

00:01:25.350 --> 00:01:30.369
Merlyn and of course Arrow the show changed
that a little so the character John Barrowman

00:01:30.369 --> 00:01:35.280
plays on the show is an amalgamation of the
old version of the character and the new version.

00:01:35.280 --> 00:01:39.159
So what does them picking a title like “The
Magician” say about the story. Mostly I

00:01:39.159 --> 00:01:43.159
think it’s going to be John Barrowman’s
grand re-introduction to starling city. They’ll

00:01:43.159 --> 00:01:47.740
have to explain what he was doing while he
was away the first time and then what he’s

00:01:47.740 --> 00:01:49.579
been doing since he came back for Thea.

00:01:49.579 --> 00:01:53.329
There’s no guarantee that Thea will be part
of the episode, but since Willa Holland is

00:01:53.329 --> 00:01:57.070
still a cast regular I’m guessing she’ll
be around. Mostly it’s going to be about

00:01:57.070 --> 00:01:57.890
Merlyn though.

00:01:57.890 --> 00:02:03.469
He’s Oliver’s ultimate nemesis, like Grant
Gustin’s Flash and Professor Zoom. Merlyn

00:02:03.469 --> 00:02:10.129
is a little more ambiguous, but what if they
gave him his own island arc. Not send Merlyn

00:02:10.129 --> 00:02:16.160
to the island, I mean give him a flashback
story that will be told over one or more episodes.

00:02:16.160 --> 00:02:19.950
Oliver’s flashbacks serve a really important
role. Yes they’re super cool, but they’re

00:02:19.950 --> 00:02:24.769
meant to inform the plot in present day. Usually
the flashbacks tease things that are central

00:02:24.769 --> 00:02:26.060
to each episode.

00:02:26.060 --> 00:02:30.170
Because episode 4 is titled The Magician,
they could use a flashback to tee up Merlyn’s

00:02:30.170 --> 00:02:35.690
grand plan for season 3. Remember in the comics,
Oliver got one up on him in an archery contest

00:02:35.690 --> 00:02:39.099
shaming him big time. So the show could twist
that theme and do a flashback explaining where

00:02:39.099 --> 00:02:43.790
Merlyn sulked off to in disgrace after season
1 and then in present day have him set up

00:02:43.790 --> 00:02:50.790
a plot to get one up on Oliver in some big
way.

00:02:51.650 --> 00:02:56.239
Usually when the show picks a title that is
straight of the Comic Book Page it uses something

00:02:56.239 --> 00:02:58.129
major from an important comic book story.

00:02:58.129 --> 00:02:59.239
Arrow doesn’t ever straight up copy the
comics, they always change things a little.

00:02:59.239 --> 00:03:04.840
But the episode regardless of references will
be all about Merlyn and his new plan.

00:03:04.840 --> 00:03:08.470
There’s also the meta thing going on where
John Barrowman’s personality in real life

00:03:08.470 --> 00:03:12.370
makes me think that Malcolm Merlyn in the
episode is going to be really theatrical,

00:03:12.370 --> 00:03:18.769
like a Stage Performer. For anyone who hasn’t
seen him at a convention, John Barrowman is

00:03:18.769 --> 00:03:22.810
way over the top in the best possible way.

00:03:22.810 --> 00:03:26.670
If you remember him from Doctor Who or Torchwood
when he got to do a little more singing and

00:03:26.670 --> 00:03:30.739
dancing. That’s what I’m thinking of.
Stephen Amell already said that he refused

00:03:30.739 --> 00:03:35.610
to do a musical episode of Arrow. He was mostly
joking, but all the same Malcolm Merlyn will

00:03:35.610 --> 00:03:42.170
be flamboyant without being funny. Picture
more of Tom Hiddleston’s Loki humor and

00:03:42.170 --> 00:03:47.709
physicality. Something close to that.

00:03:47.709 --> 00:03:51.019
As for what I think he was up to during the
break. I mostly think he was training Thea

00:03:51.019 --> 00:03:55.799
and laying the groundwork for a takeover plan.
Something that would restore a lot of his

00:03:55.799 --> 00:03:59.860
lost power. Remember, he lost his company
just like Oliver lost his company. So Merlyn

00:03:59.860 --> 00:04:02.280
and Oliver share a lot in common.

00:04:02.280 --> 00:04:07.319
Thea is a little easier to predict. I have
no idea what Merlyn’s plan is going to be

00:04:07.319 --> 00:04:11.680
other than it will involve him taking advantage
of a very distracted Oliver.

00:04:11.680 --> 00:04:16.060
Willa Holland posted this picture to instagram
recently. It’s just her working with a hardcore

00:04:16.060 --> 00:04:20.300
trainer. In terms of persona or comic book
characters, I would think she’d be closer

00:04:20.300 --> 00:04:24.640
to Artemis. They’d just change Artemis’
backstory the way they changed Isobel Rochev

00:04:24.640 --> 00:04:27.890
to make her Ravager.
And if you needed more evidence, don’t forget

00:04:27.890 --> 00:04:31.270
that Thea had archery trophies in her bedroom.

00:04:31.270 --> 00:04:35.610
Her motivation is a little unclear, but I
can’t wait to see her and Roy get a big

00:04:35.610 --> 00:04:39.260
fight scene.

00:04:39.260 --> 00:04:43.990
And when I mentioned Oliver being distracted,
I was mostly referring to the new villains,

00:04:43.990 --> 00:04:49.110
Count Vertigo and Ra’s Al Ghul occupying
the biggest part of his head and his other

00:04:49.110 --> 00:04:53.040
remainin brain cells being spent thinking
about Felicity, Ray Palmer and everyone else.

00:04:53.040 --> 00:04:57.320
It just seems like Merlyn would use that situation
to take advantage of Oliver.

00:04:57.320 --> 00:05:04.320
So now, just to explain Zatanna, Doctor Fate
and magic inside the Arrow Verse. It doesn’t

00:05:04.800 --> 00:05:11.110
exist right now. But the producers of the
DC TV shows are all open to crossovers. So

00:05:11.110 --> 00:05:15.050
until there’s a strong plan in place for
Arrow and Constantine to start referencing

00:05:15.050 --> 00:05:20.180
each other. Zatanna has a better chance of
showing up inside a Constantine episode.

00:05:20.180 --> 00:05:26.670
And based on the Doctor Fate teaser in the
premiere. It seems like they’re not going

00:05:26.670 --> 00:05:32.280
full on with big DC Superhero cameos just
yet. They’ll probably follow the Arrow model.

00:05:32.280 --> 00:05:37.640
Stick to core characters the first season
and if it gets renewed. Use season 2 to bring

00:05:37.640 --> 00:05:42.220
in more comic book characters. Zatanna would
just be a really easy sell. Constantine already

00:05:42.220 --> 00:05:44.810
sells the idea of magic and supernatural powers.

00:05:44.810 --> 00:05:50.450
In case you missed it, Guillermo Del Toro
still has the Justice League Dark script in

00:05:50.450 --> 00:05:56.930
development and he said he’d totally make
Constantine part of the team. That doesn’t

00:05:56.930 --> 00:05:59.290
mean it’s going to happen, but think about
this.

00:05:59.290 --> 00:06:03.950
The tv shows and the movies won’t have any
crossover, so consider them separate universes.

00:06:03.950 --> 00:06:08.990
I think the chances are pretty good we could
see a tv version of Justice League Dark before

00:06:08.990 --> 00:06:14.550
they ever tried it as a movie. Plus via Arrow
and The Flash they can do a modified Justice

00:06:14.550 --> 00:06:14.860
Society.

00:06:14.860 --> 00:06:20.980
That way they can stay away from the movie
characters and still do the big team up.

00:06:20.980 --> 00:06:24.270
They’re just getting started with The Flash
so I don’t expect anything like that for

00:06:24.270 --> 00:06:27.690
at least another season or two. But if they
did it on Smallville, they can totally do

00:06:27.690 --> 00:06:28.490
it again.

00:06:28.490 --> 00:06:34.980
Let me know if you would rather see Justice
League Dark done on tv first. And do you think

00:06:34.980 --> 00:06:39.450
Arrow and The Flash will get to Justice Society
before Zack Snyder and the movie people get

00:06:39.450 --> 00:06:40.820
to Justice League?

00:06:40.820 --> 00:06:44.980
I say yes to both. Justice League Dark on
tv is a no brainer, Guillermo Del Toro always

00:06:44.980 --> 00:06:49.360
seems like the busiest man on the planet and
he’s developing Pacific Rim 2, so he might

00:06:49.360 --> 00:06:54.190
not be able to participate if it happens.
But the Justice League movie isn’t planned

00:06:54.190 --> 00:06:59.790
till 2017. That’s almost season 6 of Arrow.
I definitely think that Flash and Arrow can

00:06:59.790 --> 00:07:00.980
get there first.

00:07:00.980 --> 00:07:06.410
I’m planning on doing a video for my Favorite
Justice League Dark stories and Justice Society.

00:07:06.410 --> 00:07:12.940
Be sure to subscribe to get those. There has
been some movie news recently. Mostly that

00:07:12.940 --> 00:07:18.580
Lex Luthor is going to clone a kryptonian
at the end of Batman vs Superman and synthesize

00:07:18.580 --> 00:07:25.580
kryptonite. That’s just a rumor but I’ll
do a video if it turns into something bigger.

